  "statement": "Factorise $x^{4}+4$ as a product of two quadratics with integer coefficients, and verify your factorisation.",
  "solution": "Using the Sophie Germain identity $a^{4}+4b^{4}=(a^{2}+2b^{2}+2ab)(a^{2}+2b^{2}-2ab)$ with $a=x,b=1$: $x^{4}+4=(x^{2}+2+2x)(x^{2}+2-2x)=(x^{2}+2x+2)(x^{2}-2x+2)$. Expanding: $(x^{2}+2x+2)(x^{2}-2x+2)=x^{4}-2x^{3}+2x^{2}+2x^{3}-4x^{2}+4x+2x^{2}-4x+4=x^{4}+4$.",
  "hints": [
    "Write $x^{4}+4$ as $x^{4}+4x^{2}+4-4x^{2}$.",
    "Recognise a difference of two squares."
  ],
